STATEMENT 3: InsertProductAsync
================================================================================

ORIGINAL SQL SERVER STATEMENT:
DECLARE @NewProductId INT;

BEGIN TRANSACTION;
    -- Insert the new product
    INSERT INTO Products (Name, Description, Price, StockQuantity)
    VALUES (@Name, @Description, @Price, @StockQuantity);
    
    SET @NewProductId = SCOPE_IDENTITY();
    
    -- Log the insertion
    INSERT INTO ProductHistory (ProductId, Action, OldPrice, NewPrice, OldStock, NewStock, ActionDate)
    VALUES (@NewProductId, 'INSERT', NULL, @Price, NULL, @StockQuantity, GETDATE());
    
    -- Update product statistics
    UPDATE ProductStats
    SET 
        TotalProducts = TotalProducts + 1,
        AveragePrice = (AveragePrice * TotalProducts + @Price) / (TotalProducts + 1),
        LastUpdated = GETDATE()
    WHERE StatId = 1;
COMMIT;

SELECT @NewProductId;

DMS TOOL OUTPUT:
Not attempted due to consistent timeout pattern from previous statements.

MANUAL CONVERSION APPLIED:
- Replaced SCOPE_IDENTITY() with RETURNING clause on INSERT
- Replaced GETDATE() with CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
- Converted multi-statement transaction to use CTEs for data flow
- Used RETURNING clause to capture new ProductId
- Note: This will need to be executed as separate statements within a transaction in C# code

POSTGRESQL CONVERTED STATEMENT:
WITH inserted_product AS (
    INSERT INTO Products (Name, Description, Price, StockQuantity)
    VALUES (@Name, @Description, @Price, @StockQuantity)
    RETURNING ProductId
),
log_insert AS (
    INSERT INTO ProductHistory (ProductId, Action, OldPrice, NewPrice, OldStock, NewStock, ActionDate)
    SELECT ProductId, 'INSERT', NULL, @Price, NULL, @StockQuantity, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
    FROM inserted_product
    RETURNING ProductId
)
UPDATE ProductStats
SET 
    TotalProducts = TotalProducts + 1,
    AveragePrice = (AveragePrice * TotalProducts + @Price) / (TotalProducts + 1),
    LastUpdated = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
WHERE StatId = 1
RETURNING (SELECT ProductId FROM inserted_product);

